            "The term fiduciary has a particular legal history in domestic systems, where duties arise from recognized relationships, statutes, or other sources of law. A diplomat may have obligations to the state they represent under domestic law and official duties, but that does not automatically make every negotiator a trustee of a bilateral relationship or create a legally enforceable fiduciary duty owed by one sovereign to another. The Chancellery's use of fiduciary language is a normative proposal for responsible practice unless a specific legal instrument independently gives it binding effect.",
