        "The Chancellery Fiduciary Standard is an internal ethical framework for examining whether a proposed agreement creates foreseeable risks to institutional capacity, essential services, or the rights of affected people. It asks negotiators to disclose material trade-offs and consider whether a bargain's implementation is practicable and consistent with applicable law. It does not give a negotiator unilateral authority to reject a state policy or create a general fiduciary duty between sovereigns.",
