            "The assessment of viability should be evidence-based and context-specific. Relevant dimensions may include fiscal capacity, access to essential services, institutional continuity, food and energy security, public health, rights protections, and the ability to administer the agreement. These indicators do not form a universal checklist or a single score unless the authorized framework says so. A government's budget constraint, for example, cannot by itself establish that it will collapse; analysts must examine data, competing explanations, and the time horizon.",
