            "Negotiation analysis sometimes calls the best available alternative to a negotiated agreement a BATNA. This is a strategic planning concept, not a legal status or a prediction of what a party will choose. A BATNA is only useful if it is feasible, authorized, and understood by the people who would implement it. A theoretical military option or an unapproved budget plan should not be treated as a credible alternative merely because it appears on a negotiating slide.",
